source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Jira reads its dash rule at a list item's content start and draws the rule inside the item, so jiro writes the rule as the item's own block; `- ***` is the JFM spelling, because a line of dashes alone would be a thematic break of its own rather than an item.
-- input.jira --
* ----
-- rendered.html --
<ul>
	<li><hr /></li>
</ul>
-- want.md --
- ***
-- warnings.json --
[]
